# ---- Personnel data: real names/IDs, never commit ----
# (source roster spreadsheets and the CSV/SQL seed files
# scripts/build_technician_seed.py generates from them for Supabase import)
*roster*.xlsx
*Plant_Access*.xlsx
technicians_seed.csv
technician_plant_access_seed.csv
technicians_seed.sql
technician_plant_access_seed.sql

# ---- Real mix design workbooks: reference only, carry real names ----
# Legacy MixPack .xls/.xlsm files are dropped in docs/ to map fields against
# (see docs/legacy-mixpack-map.md). They hold technician SM IDs, contractor
# and plant names, etc. — authoritative data lives in Supabase, not here.
docs/*.xls
docs/*.xlsx
docs/*.xlsm
MIXPACK*.xls*
\#*.xls*
# Completed AMAW (plant acceptance) workbooks carry technician names, contract
# and plant data the same way.
AMAW*.xls*
# ...except KYTC's own blank templates, which are public downloads off their
# SiteManager page and hold no data. Each generator needs one as the base it
# writes into, so they have to be served, not just referenced. AMAW 14.01 is
# the current public download; Jake's two real lots are 13.3, and all 85
# dictionary rows and every staging dimension are identical across 13.3 /
# 13.04 / 14.01 (docs/amaw-map.md), so the newer template is the right base
# for a lot checked against the older files.
!public/MIXPACK2026_VER12_01.xlsm
!public/AMAW_VER14_01.xlsm

